4.31, near the middle of its 2718.09-2795 range, so immediate follow-through above the spike high is unconfirmed.", "A prior spike at bar 59 to 2680 also failed to hold; price subsequently dropped to 2358.62, showing that sharp bull spikes in this window have not always led to sustained trends.", "The window spent most of its bars in overlapping ranges (bars 18-58 and 59-100), so the current trend is relatively young and could still be a breakout attempt within a larger range.", "The latest leg from 2495.82 to 2850 is steep and may be climactic; if price falls back below 2658.06 or 2568.16, the higher-low sequence would be challenged.", "The large upper tail on bar 118 can attract profit-taking and lead to a trading range or pullback rather than continued one-way buying."], "evidence_for": ["Higher swing lows since the 2358.62 bar 84 low: 2370.54, 2435.71, 2495.82, 2568.16, 2658.06.", "Higher highs: 2495.99, 2519.81, 2585.50, 2643.52, 2700.00, 2850.00, with the latest high above the prior 2680.00 spike high.", "Recent bull bars are large and close near their highs (e.g., bar 101 close 2578.60 after 2507.15 open; bar 102 close 2636.28; bar 118 close 2723.15 after 2658.81 open).", "Pullbacks in the latest leg were bought: bars 110-112 pulled back to 2568.16 but did not break below the bar 101 low of 2495.82, and bars 113-116 resumed upward.", "The close at 2754.31 is above the 2700.00 prior swing highs (bars 106 and 116) and above the 2680.00 bar 59 spike high, indicating acceptance above old resistance."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window covers 120 closed H4 bars; overall low is 2357.18 (bar 4) and overall high is 2850 (bar 118), with the last close at 2754.31.", "Early bars sold off from 2451.95 to 2357.18, then recovered to 2537.57 (bar 16 high) before bar 17 reversed sharply lower from 2527.18 to close 2450.96.", "Bars 18-58 overlapped heavily between 2411.04 (bar 53 low) and 2537.57/2528.8, with repeated failures to sustain moves above 2520 an